# Baseline for plugins/core scan.
# The injection detector fires on "allowlist" in skills/harden/SKILL.md — a
# known false positive from security documentation that uses the word "allowlist"
# in a context the permission-escalation pattern matches. Documented limitation
# in policy.sh: "best-effort, not a security boundary."
#
# Format: relative-path<TAB>rule
# This file is operator-supplied (--baseline flag). Never place it inside the
# scanned plugin directory — a plugin that controls its own baseline can suppress
# any finding against itself.
skills/harden/SKILL.md	permission-escalation
